tatements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${∬}_{D}(3x-y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,2]\\times [-4,1]$\n- **II.** ${∬}_{R}(3x-y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-4,4]$\n- **III.** ${∬}_{D}(3x-y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-4,0]$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](images/a7/a7af801fa9975dda6ce3b12b2cde2c328721cd5e0affd16f1a14ab26cfa21bdd.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}(3x-y), & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(3x-y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statements I is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement II is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statements III is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054632 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "495f3da0-849a-589d-ac88-26d6825445e4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Subsets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc8ced0a-ba6f-5ad7-88c0-9ebf46c62208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451795} {:answer/id #uuid "342e13e3-9800-53cf-9366-d3c87a489b4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc8ced0a-ba6f-5ad7-88c0-9ebf46c62208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451795} :answer-field/id #uuid "571944e4-b535-51ab-92d3-6cdb09493a7a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452745} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1126e9e0-8232-5d35-8038-8bf328ded170" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451797} {:answer/id #uuid "615a2768-0749-5412-a7db-f09acc474a5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "615a2768-0749-5412-a7db-f09acc474a5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451798} :answer-field/id #uuid "abf90b77-7bc6-5618-b11c-374e8a2add6f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452746} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b212baa9-6aa5-509c-9b0f-258b4ef85f55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451799} {:answer/id #uuid "73feb374-98b9-585c-8aba-c90f06e91ed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73feb374-98b9-585c-8aba-c90f06e91ed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451800} :answer-field/id #uuid "38c2d820-d8fc-578d-a1ab-2c25f2897ba2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f0cc03e-26f5-51bc-b8ad-bdb1b8cf7d61" :question/math-academy-id "q-80832" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={x\\in N:1\\le x<6}$ and $B={x\\in N:3x<9}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A⊆B$\n- **II.** $B⊆A$\n- **III.** $A⊈B$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all natural numbers greater than or equal to $1$ but less than $6.$ So,\n\n$$\nA={1,2,3,4,5}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are natural numbers which satisfy the inequality $3x<9.$ So,\n\n$$\nB={1,2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊆B$ is false, while $A⊈B$ is true. For example, $5\\in A$ but $5\\notin B.$\n\n- $B⊆A$ is true. Every element in the set $B$ is an element of the set $A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054632 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "495f3da0-849a-589d-ac88-26d6825445e4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Subsets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c94151ca-d0d0-5c0a-9142-2d9e3bbdf24c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451801} {:answer/id #uuid "b63ee5cf-27b9-5337-82e1-5f492db4a72e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c94151ca-d0d0-5c0a-9142-2d9e3bbdf24c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451801} :answer-field/id #uuid "64224f0b-584b-59b9-9aa9-96918c898c62" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452748} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec08aaf9-9d96-5ea6-b0b4-c472fe416aa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451803} {:answer/id #uuid "a321fa62-5e61-53ab-94ec-ba3ba9892960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a321fa62-5e61-53ab-94ec-ba3ba9892960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451804} :answer-field/id #uuid "a51f3693-e502-5224-bb23-05134e129548" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452749} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09c3a9bc-5d80-5f5f-b63c-998493639335" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451805} {:answer/id #uuid "67243169-62b8-5e91-b25a-6a53cecb1b2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451806}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09c3a9bc-5d80-5f5f-b63c-998493639335" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451805} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d09f76c-3a00-52e9-82e2-d4ddd8f9c8a5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c643dbca-796e-5e8a-ae4e-2697e41e25d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-80837" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={x\\in {Z}^{+}∣x\\le 3}$ and $B={x\\in Z∣0\\le x<3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A⊆B$\n- **II.** $B⊈A$\n- **III.** $∅⊈B$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all positive integers that satisfy the inequality $x\\le 3.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nA={1,2,3}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are all integers that satisfy the inequality $0\\le x<3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nB={0,1,2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊆B$ is false. For example, $3\\in A$ but $3\\notin B.$\n\n- $B⊈A$ is true. For example, $0\\in B$ but $0\\notin A.$\n\n- $∅⊈B$ is false. The null set $∅={}$ is a subset of *every* set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054632 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "495f3da0-849a-589d-ac88-26d6825445e4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Subsets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd183097-a404-5feb-952a-2387b100d23e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451807} {:answer/id #uuid "94030ec2-e77c-5e81-83f3-5026503525a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94030ec2-e77c-5e81-83f3-5026503525a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451808} :answer-field/id #uuid "16a854c1-f276-5aa3-841d-8cfe4d3ed38b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452751} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a18f6937-d520-5613-9309-e9c169d33c50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451809} {:answer/id #uuid "46aa31ca-9b95-5fbc-b4ec-a1024e21fa1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 