alue "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451991} {:answer/id #uuid "01f64f3a-256c-5b22-a4f9-411d66aeef70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01f64f3a-256c-5b22-a4f9-411d66aeef70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451992} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc95f6fb-f3c0-5b76-b045-537413682258" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6847dae1-289b-5050-b4ae-95ca49b57e85" :question/math-academy-id "q-94632" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $L$ containing all polynomials of degree exactly $1.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $L$ is closed under function addition\n\n- **II.** $L$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\n- **III.** $L$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n\n- **IV.** $L$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $f(x)=x$ and $g(x)=1-x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)+g(x) & =x+(1-x) \\\\  & =(x-x)+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $L$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(x)=x$ and $k=0,$ then\n\n$$\nkf(x)=0\\cdot x=0.\n$$\n\n \nSo, $L$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $L$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360466 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b09ea6bd-4607-5a1a-b61d-0e02b0c80e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451993} {:answer/id #uuid "cd2d3ef5-c550-52ac-941d-400c951777cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b09ea6bd-4607-5a1a-b61d-0e02b0c80e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451993} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c9e456f-6a38-5535-a752-f5054096da9b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "156331ef-d3cc-5f8a-ab05-d5f83ec4fc97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451995} {:answer/id #uuid "daefc99f-010a-5738-9ce2-c841ee85a71f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "156331ef-d3cc-5f8a-ab05-d5f83ec4fc97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451995} :answer-field/id #uuid "c71a05b2-f839-5b7f-b46a-90b60bd5f8e9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc1167eb-dbeb-5114-80a3-93921f4a107f" :answer/type {: