**II.** $Q$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\n- **III.** $Q$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n\n- **IV.** $Q$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $f(x)={x}^{2}$ and $g(x)=-{x}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nf(x)+g(x)={x}^{2}+(-{x}^{2})=0.\n$$\n\nSo, $Q$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(x)={x}^{2}$ and $k=0,$ then\n\n$$\nkf(x)=0\\cdot {x}^{2}=0.\n$$\n\n \nSo, $Q$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $Q$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360467 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb2d723d-c8b0-5e00-b156-69d0e470f0ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452001} {:answer/id #uuid "5b1f3a41-57bb-56b5-b700-a05f59bcdb05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb2d723d-c8b0-5e00-b156-69d0e470f0ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452001} :answer-field/id #uuid "eaed178b-0ca9-53db-93f2-6c3fe7166a1e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452848} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02d54602-