a167ab0d-34f6-5000-8bef-7f7a8ae3ed10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452008} :answer-field/id #uuid "1aa85b89-bf70-5661-b433-3d5ffe0aa95a" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0f62d508-5cf6-5993-b139-949d11db546e" :question/math-academy-id "q-94635" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $C$ containing all polynomials of degree exactly $3.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $C$ is closed under function addition\n- **II.** $C$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $C$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n- **IV.** $C$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $f(x)={x}^{3}$ and $g(x)=1-{x}^{3},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)+g(x) & ={x}^{3}+(1-{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =({x}^{3}-{x}^{3})+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $C$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(x)={x}^{3}$ and $k=0,$ then\n\n$$\nkf(x)=0\\cdot {x}^{3}=0.\n$$\n\n \nSo, $C$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $C$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360468 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "991f2f73-ac23-5191-ab80-7de9efee7e9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452009} {:answer/id #uuid "2ead1013-7e82-50d2-9ea0-c2b7d5a04066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ead1013-7e82-50d2-9ea0-c2b7d5a04066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452010} :answer-field/id #uuid "506cf49e-9f52-5299-8ed3-6ff8e24478db" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452852} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fed6d2ec-aee8-5542-8372-ae559f20b93f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452011} {:answer/id #uuid "c05c0c3e-d50a-5489-b880-65368c86a869" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c05c0c3e-d50a-5489-b880-65368c86a869" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452012} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b6ad786-f4e4-5537-b235-5beb1d76d0c8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452853} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e1613e4-3825-5163-955a-c508dc5a7424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452013} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a4d7ea-1e52-5939-b1ad-c82fa09897e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5a4d7ea-1e52-5939-b1ad-c82fa09897e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452014} :answer-field/id #uuid "860bab32-e063-5c7b-9daf-21735a207ce5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452854} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "902ecaea-e103-52f1-8446-e92ffd5c7e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452015} {:answer/id #uuid "b5359c31-2887-5291-8d2f-9c2c74acea93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "902ecaea-e103-52f1-8446-e92ffd5c7e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452015} :answer-field/id #uuid "063b6651-61e1-5617-8f54-44670f58aa5b" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "44096d11-ac2c-5302-8668-0431e5543e9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94642" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[-2,2]$ of all continuous functions $f:[-2,2]\\to R$ and its subset $E$ containing all even functions.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $E$ is closed under function addition\n- **II.** $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $E$ is a subspace of $C[-2,2]$\n- **IV.** $E$ is **not** a subspace of $C[-2,2]$\n\n*Hint: $f$ is even if $f(-x)=f(x)$ for all $x\\in [-2,2].$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(x),g(x)\\in E,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(-x) & =f(-x)+g(-x) \\\\  & =f(x)+g(x) \\\\  & =(f+g)(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $E$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(x)\\in E$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kf)(-x) & =kf(-x) \\\\  & =kf(x) \\\\  & =(kf)(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $E$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360469 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73a902ed-7491-5586-a972-d357f55a0986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452017} {:answer/id #uuid "e02d1c16-f579-53fa-a7d0-24fb41030a0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73a902ed-7491-5586-a972-d357f55a0986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452017} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf830ad1-3967-59b5-8125-48068d769bf7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452856} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f9fc86f-cdfb-5892-81a6-1b0d9bc7eb9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452019} {:answer/id #uuid "e30cf1d6-9863-5658-be8b-c21ac4b2d15c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f9fc86f-cdfb-5892-81a6-1b0d9bc7eb9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452019} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d0d49b1-179c-5765-84f1-7b10b986b831" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452857} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23886679-356d-53bc-88ed-fee5a9a5549f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452021} {:answer/id #uuid "2e29665f-db3f-5174-adca-366e367ba005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e29665f-db3f-5174-adca-366e367ba005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452022} :answer-field/id #uuid "e539d322-ecc4-522f-b82d-d2e18147e866" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452858}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ff3e8b0-9d12-58ec-aef1-61a782559716" :question/math-academy-id "q-94649" :question/problem "Let $N$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=0.$  Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The constant function $f(x)=1$ for all $x\\in R$ belongs to $N.$\n- **II.** For any $f(t),g(t)\\in N,$ we have $f(t)-g(t)=g(t)-f(t).$\n- **III.** The addition of functions in $N$ is commutative." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $N$ contains only functions that evaluate to zero at zero. However, the function defined by $f(x)=1$ for all $x\\in R$ satisfies $f(0)=1\\ne 0.$ So, $f\\notin N.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, consider functions $f(t)=2t$ and $g(t)=t$ in $N.$ Then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)-g(t) & =2t-t \\\\  & =t \\\\ g(t)-f(t) & =t-2t \\\\  & =-t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(t)-g(t)\\ne g(t)-f(t).$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any functions $f(t),g(t)\\in N,$ we obtain that \n\n$$\nf(t)+g(t)=g(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nsince the addition of functions is commutative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360471 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "109109e7-1c69-56cd-9b2e-c839c768d3cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452023} {:answer/id #uuid "edac93af-d167-569f-a0e3-5072a6fee483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edac93af-d167-569f-a0e3-5072a6fee483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452024} :answer-field/id #uuid "b642997b-3b81-5855-8836-d3b87e046226" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452859} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca7bbf3b-be14-56ec-b1e4-11147c4bf70c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452025} {:answer/id #uuid "f10e7355-6abf-5461-9323-1738529d32f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f10e7355-6abf-5461-9323-1738529d32f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452026} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9edafdb-244a-5445-97a3-cffa0d55e2ba" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452860} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c78337cc-3bc4-5bc3-9ab8-a2d47e6765be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452027} {:answer/id #uuid "12dfbd69-08c1-535f-bfb5-4830de06751e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c78337cc-3bc4-5bc3-9ab8-a2d47e6765be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452027} :answer-field/id #uuid "df579160-ca8f-5445-a24d-a55d4ac1e168" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452861}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "998609c4-bfb7-5e7d-ad89-b03b40316ca2" :question/math-academy-id "q-94661" :question/problem "Let $F$ be the set of polynomials of the form $ax+b,$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The zero-polynomial belongs to $F.$\n\n- **II.** For the zero polynomial $0$ and any $p(x)\\in F,$ we have $p(x)+0=p(x).$\n\n- **III.** There are polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in F$ such that $p(x)+q(x)\\ne q(x)+p(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the zero-polynomial can be represented as\n\n$$\n0=0\\cdot x+0.\n$$\n\nHence, $0\\in F.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for the zero-polynomial $0$ and any $p(x)\\in F,$ we have\n\n$$\np(x)+0=p(x)\n$$\n\nsince $0$ is the unique zero element in the set of all polynomials.\n\n- Statement III is false. For any polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in F,$ we have that\n\n$$\np(x)+q(x)=q(x)+p(x)\n$$\n\nsince the addition of polynomials is commutative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360473 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "902db5be-70c1-5674-b997-99068ce5edfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452029} {:answer/id #uuid "814a1883-467d-5324-b6ef-116433356eb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "814a1883-467d-5324-b6ef-116433356eb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452030} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c08151d-a778-5873-a9ce-fddc4ab45b26" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452862} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7a65cf4-7f49-5de1-8fe2-89baa7786a6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452031} {:answer/id #uuid "e089eec9-7866-5f1a-a19f-c3d7e6029a81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7a65cf4-7f49-5de1-8fe2-89baa7786a6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452031} :answer-field/id #uuid "f698df9a-9c04-5d46-ad26-9bbf7397619f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452863} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ecbe2c7-ade2-5481-b820-bfe9f428123f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452033} {:answer/id #uuid "3ff2aef1-031d-5390-a56e-ad3f1cd32bac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ecbe2c7-ade2-5481-b820-bfe9f428123f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452033} :answer-field/id #uuid "b85432db-4f8a-59af-af6d-ee5723b311ce" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86d246c9-ffba-5c6c-b83e-58058d87e01e" :question/math-academy-id "q-94686" :question/problem "Let $E$ be the set of polynomials of the form $a{x}^{2}+1,$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The constant polynomial $1$ belongs to $E.$\n- **II.** For the constant polynomial $1$ and any $p(x)\\in E,$ we have $1+p(x)=p(x).$\n- **III.** There are polynomials $p(x),q(x),r(x)\\in E$ such that $[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)\\ne p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the constant polynomial $1$ can be represented as\n\n$$\n1=0\\cdot {x}^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nHence, $1\\in E.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, consider the polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}+1\\in E.$ Then, \n\n$$\n1+p(x)=1+{x}^{2}+1={x}^{2}+2\\ne p(x).\n$$\n\nThe zero-polynomial $0$ is the unique polynomial such that for any $p(x)\\in E$ we have $0+p(x)=p(x).$\n\n- Statement III is false. For any polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in E,$ we have \n\n$$\n[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)=p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)],\n$$\n\nsince polynomial addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360475 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc6bcc99-b3af-511c-91ae-c4f89185a51b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452035} {:answer/id #uuid "4f2702cc-0039-5cff-ab51-3043f6c2744c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f2702cc-0039-5cff-ab51-3043f6c2744c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452036} :answer-field/id #uuid "649a81e0-ac77-5ec9-ae54-66f470930379" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452865} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b185955a-71e1-5cda-8cd9-a2fd6aaac544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452037} {:answer/id #uuid "38bb6b6b-c279-54ab-994d-20b82f110997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b185955a-71e1-5cda-8cd9-a2fd6aaac544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452037} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac94e2aa-cdd1-5e7c-b142-37d6eab761ea" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452866} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bf0ebb4-415a-54f5-9321-bd974e7046ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452039} {:answer/id #uuid "36b27cb9-c8ff-51e8-ad54-c9c26a9e4d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36b27cb9-c8ff-51e8-ad54-c9c26a9e4d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452040} :answer-field/id #uuid "27b49265-285f-512b-aebb-320dd01bc0ad" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452867}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d30a6a74-1882-58de-a0e8-caf74485928f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94700" :question/problem "Let $R$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** For any $A\\in R,$ we have $1\\cdot A=A.$\n\n- **II.** For any $A\\in R,$ we have $-1(-1\\cdot A)=-A.$\n\n- **III.** For any $A\\in R$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in R$ with real entries, we have\n\n$$\n1\\cdot {a}_{ij}={a}_{ij}\n$$\n\nand, hence,\n\n$$\n1\\cdot A=A.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ from $R.$  Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1(-1\\cdot A) & =-1(-1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =-1([\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot 1 & (-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 0 & (-1)\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =-1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-1) & (-1)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 0 & (-1)\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =A\\ne -A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statements III is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in R,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta ){a}_{ij}=\\alpha {a}_{ij}+\\beta {a}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1474a3e2-e736-5b19-b171-2993227de350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452041} {:answer/id #uuid "9b98079f-fe90-5caa-80dc-7270db379b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1474a3e2-e736-5b19-b171-2993227de350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" 