:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "db8c1e1e-2555-50dd-bb83-7ef5667f1f43" :question/math-academy-id "q-94781" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3},{v}_{3}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent\n- **II.** ${2{v}_{1},{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent\n- **III.** ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+1\\cdot ({v}_{2}-{v}_{3})+1\\cdot ({v}_{3}-{v}_{1})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2}-{v}_{3})+{x}_{3}({v}_{3}-{v}_{1})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3},{v}_{3}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2{v}_{1})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2})+{x}_{3}(3{v}_{3}) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}_{1}){v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+(3{x}_{3}){v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{2{v}_{1},{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement III is false.  If ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0$ has a non-zero solution, $a\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{2}=0,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\na\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{2}+0\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4105f1cb-eb48-5946-92f7-cd5e67689912" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type by Calculating the Corresponding Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f98de070-157f-534d-80ca-0285e5ea31dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452083} {:answer/id #uuid "174de886-386b-5d7b-a04e-97378dcc50c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "174de886-386b-5d7b-a04e-97378dcc50c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452084} :answer-field/id #uuid "e799f149-b778-5e67-89e1-41f4feb99d40" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452889} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e4d1217-ff6e-508b-b3bc-dea5acc63146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452085} {:answer/id #uuid "78c882b5-c654-506d-9f34-f6de960b4eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78c882b5-c654-506d-9f34-f6de960b4eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452086} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb439c2a-82f5-579a-b442-b6cef060ee5e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452890} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dbe70c7-c5db-5456-9d9f-eceb402243d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452087} {:answer/id #uuid "7f3f8a7a-53c9-58ba-8c93-06d4c7b15b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0dbe70c7-c5db-5456-9d9f-eceb402243d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452087} :answer-field/id #uuid "b68b3e83-f797-507a-a054-d24715a897e1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13d1d5cf-031d-5ebf-8e4c-d550f344afdd" :question/math-academy-id "q-94795" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The eigenvalues of $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=5$\n- **II.** ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite\n- **III.** $A$ is indefinite" :question/worked-solution "Given a quadratic form $Q(x)={x}^{T}Ax,$ we have the following theorem:\n\n- $Q$ is positive-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are positive,\n\n- $Q$ is positive semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-negative (note that positive semi-definite quadratic forms include all positive-definite quadratic forms),\n\n- $Q$ is negative-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are negative,\n\n- $Q$ is negative semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-positive (note that negative semi-definite quadratic forms include all negative-definite quadratic forms), and\n\n- $Q$ is indefinite if and only if $A$ has both positive and negative eigenvalues.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the characteristic equation of $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +5 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =1,\\,5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. Since all the eigenvalues of $A$ are positive, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is positive-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbebdd1b-0716-55cb-8df6-12a35b517ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e6b6069-a73e-55b4-8237-8d4f4f222dac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452089} {:answer/id #uuid "db8fa190-5652-57d4-9d6f-36a68e1d279f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db8fa190-5652-57d4-9d6f-36a68e1d279f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452090} :answer-field/id #uuid "88f61762-6f70-5d21-b1c1-800aae0f2fff" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452892} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "311261b6-23c6-5a90-af11-2891a6bef398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452091} {:answer/id #uuid "3e682b91-127f-5abb-bc3a-e837723de4b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e682b91-127f-5abb-bc3a-e837723de4b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452092} :answer-field/id #uuid "4558c17e-723a-50fc-8a86-1acb9b4e8d09" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452893} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bedbf47f-c0ac-5fc5-a3f5-ee511e9a5b73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452093} {:answer/id #uuid "1a766f1d-8b11-5027-b338-059d385649a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a766f1d-8b11-5027-b338-059d385649a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452094} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdfd5bb3-65c5-50b4-abd6-2525ca2c0e80" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "81d008a7-fd35-5fff-9f9d-fc0e8e60bfec" :question/math-academy-id "q-94797" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${a}_{11}=-3$ and $det(A)=2$\n- **II.** ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is negative-definite\n- **III.** $A$ is negative-definite" :question/worked-solution "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-3$ and \n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=2.\n$$\n\n- Statements II and III are true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-3<0, \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=2>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x,$ and the matrix $A,$ are negative-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360501 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbebdd1b-0716-55cb-8df6-12a35b517ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7c44634-60fd-5951-9be7-dc5e18e58c42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452095} {:answer/id #uuid "82947ba0-932e-5c2a-99e6-18adae0f5f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82947ba0-932e-5c2a-99e6-18adae0f5f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452096} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e7037ca-26f7-5e95-8a8e-f723accdd59c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452895} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d96d178d-0a79-56c3-adbb-d837a0ce5c0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452097} {:answer/id #uuid "209120dd-a131-5d7f-a15d-2260c86df364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "209120dd-a131-5d7f-a15d-2260c86df364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452098} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3df2f8e-756f-5787-8a56-44336769a7ad" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452896} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40074442-c36f-5a79-91a2-f79a296cd176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452099} {:answer/id #uuid "c6bd9379-6e9a-5303-ba4e-5e2e9f7337ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40074442-c36f-5a79-91a2-f79a296cd176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452099} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9ef70e7-a300-569b-994b-335f8013913f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "95ed5c64-873a-5214-9b7f-9e356847bad2" :question/math-academy-id "q-94801" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${a}_{11}=6$ and $det(A)=17$\n- **II.** ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite\n- **III.** $A$ is negative-definite" :question/worked-solution "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=6$ and \n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=17.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=6>0, \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=17>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x,$ and the matrix $A,$ are positive-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360502 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbebdd1b-0716-55cb-8df6-12a35b517ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "420ec396-a215-5051-bcb8-10ed9acc95ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452101} {:answer/id #uuid "d7c27e94-c52e-5c96-8d89-053964a8a2d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "420ec396-a215-5051-bcb8-10ed9acc95ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452101} :answer-field/id #uuid "83818ab7-8e39-5903-9ee3-959ef2554040" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452898} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c441b03-7a1e-59f5-9515-8053ce5355d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452103} {:answer/id #uuid "cd8eaa01-f5f3-50e0-9b13-165b38fc8277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd8eaa01-f5f3-50e0-9b13-165b38fc8277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452104} :answer-field/id #uuid "82bbe034-c71c-5eb5-aefd-fd09fd107a27" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452899} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "897837ee-7319-5a6c-a781-a2bf0d97f197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452105} {:answer/id #uuid "317ed741-0f0a-53c2-9948-7ac37ceef348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "317ed741-0f0a-53c2-9948-7ac37ceef348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452106} :answer-field/id #uuid "536fbf80-08b5-5e1a-a2ac-b0eae9c1cf2c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "43115d1d-8694-5a95-b413-4600fbd2bc68" :question/math-academy-id "q-94804" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${a}_{11}=-5$ and $det(A)>0$\n- **II.** ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is negative-definite\n- **III.** $A$ is negative-definite" :question/worked-solution "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-5$ but \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-8)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-8<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statements II and III are true. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-5<0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|=1>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=-8<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x,$ and the matrix $A,$ are negative-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360503 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbebdd1b-0716-55cb-8df6-12a35b517ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e082f9d-d667-53bf-8ebe-ea0165b6dc26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452107} {:answer/id #uuid "1b961c92-afa7-5358-90fd-24c675c9bd2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452108}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e082f9d-d667-53bf-8ebe-ea0165b6dc26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452107} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3d091f6-4c30-55e8-95e8-5336bea05763" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452901} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e233fee2-70e2-5e90-896f-04fbc826023e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452109} {:answer/id #uuid "a851a8d9-1e67-5532-b8dd-92c9d9b65acc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a851a8d9-1e67-5532-b8dd-92c9d9b65acc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452110} :answer-field/id #uuid "3be5e419-a12d-5643-8194-2d9a2b4897ec" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452902} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0fe63a9-b90e-5777-b826-3d8827fd649a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452111} {:answer/id #uuid "1aded71f-8051-53a7-97fa-e199f9608ed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0fe63a9-b90e-5777-b826-3d8827fd649a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452111} :answer-field/id #uuid "42458164-cc6a-5528-9e47-6288386413d8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7d5f731a-8eca-5400-88d7-dd10fc541120" :question/math-academy-id "q-94805" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${a}_{11}=8$ and $det(A)<0$\n- **II.** ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite\n- **III.** $A$ is negative-definite" :question/worked-solution "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=8$ but \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =21>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=8>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}|=7>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=21>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x,$ and the matrix $A,$ are positive-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbebdd1b-0716-55cb-8df6-12a35b517ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fea1b93a-38ba-5c72-9bee-3fbe580f05cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452113} {:answer/id #uuid "81ba5de2-4ec0-55fe-bab8-33d6d9253f04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81ba5de2-4ec0-55fe-bab8-33d6d9253f04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452114} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f57c56b-b2e1-58e7-8141-026fa0dded98" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452904} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85c12093-8dda-5103-9819-5b62a8cc94b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452115} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e0ca83-7bc5-54f5-b90f-2bcba9b76ad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85c12093-8dda-5103-9819-5b62a8cc94b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452115} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dc9ccf9-fe82-5943-aefd-c2e968dec187" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452905} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c2dacb8-3a73-5142-9d28-821696fba02d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452117} {:answer/id #uuid "07437bee-0a6c-5947-bc81-ab31e28f0bc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07437bee-0a6c-5947-bc81-ab31e28f0bc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452118} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa4392f3-f738-5e5a-88d9-29ab52adafd4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452906}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b0bcde67-e6f1-5859-87e0-ff664264d2ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-94806" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${a}_{11}=-6$ and $det(A)<0$\n- **II.** ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite\n- **III.** $A$ is negative-definite" :question/worked-solution "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-6$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-6<0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}|=2>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=-6<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x,$ and the matrix $A,$ are negative-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124592 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2588e089-4786-5346-b42d-65c2740ae2ab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Sets of Vectors in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7a78d68-722c-5a86-b81e-827cf73ccb37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452119} {:answer/id #uuid "a8a1217b-b1b2-5202-a376-a348a355e361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8a1217b-b1b2-5202-a376-a348a355e361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452120} :answer-field/id #uuid "9515649f-9e44-5f61-baf3-729a68b97e8f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452907} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ef00e12-99c9-5c1c-9218-6b68325b5421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452121} {:answer/id #uuid "d6062610-898a-5fd9-8ec5-6314be543eb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ef00e12-99c9-5c1c-9218-6b68325b5421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452121} :answer-field/id #uuid "e447197c-21d9-5c73-8c22-d8a7a3296c07" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452908} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afe34d36-0fc3-563c-99d1-5708c805ab24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452123} {:answer/id #uuid "817f57a8-cd7f-5f80-806a-8559489f4936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afe34d36-0fc3-563c-99d1-5708c805ab24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452123} :answer-field/id #uuid "3906ed8a-b774-5d53-89da-c40c1ef74db1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ac8aaff6-9636-552f-aae2-acac5b76a9ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-94842" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{2}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ over $R$ with degrees at most $2.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\{t,{t}^{2}\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{2}[t]$\n\n- **II.** ${t}^{2}+1$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{t,{t}^{2}\\}$\n\n- **III.** $\\{t,{t}^{2}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}_{2}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the equation \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot t+{x}_{2}\\cdot {t}^{2}=0,\n$$\n\n \nis true if and only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ So, the set is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that all linear combinations of\n\n$$\n\\{t,{t}^{2}\\}\n$$\n\nresult in polynomials without the constant term.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, the polynomial ${t}^{2}+1$ can't be written as a linear combination of the set  $\\{t,{t}^{2}\\}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360514 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124592 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2588e089-4786-5346-b42d-65c2740ae2ab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Sets of Vectors in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87bb7a98-c575-525d-8f21-d662b93264ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452125} {:answer/id #uuid "f6638003-0464-5af5-afcf-6702ac0d7091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87bb7a98-c575-525d-8f21-d662b93264ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452125} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e9560bd-6ef4-547a-aa9e-0ec4d9c593f8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452910} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efcbc953-bb2d-59f8-9561-a8ac02a13abb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452127} {:answer/id #uuid "8374fd32-fbbf-5c22-85a2-c10487c1ebef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8374fd32-fbbf-5c22-85a2-c10487c1ebef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452128} :answer-field/id #uuid "37480e60-0e2c-59f9-b4be-acf090307d33" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452911} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f960d13-12c8-5bda-af69-0504f05800fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452129} {:answer/id #uuid "a61bf577-c31b-58b3-8d5f-774c53b573f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f960d13-12c8-5bda-af69-0504f05800fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452129} :answer-field/id #uuid "f82a5777-196c-533d-8aea-43409b51076b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452912}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d8792da5-8116-548d-a9e9-a07944635528" :question/math-academy-id "q-94847" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{3}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ over $R$ with degrees at most $3.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\{0,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{3}[t]$\n\n- **II.** $3{t}^{2}-t$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{0,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$\n\n- **III.** $\\{0,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}_{3}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot t+0\\cdot {t}^{2}+0\\cdot {t}^{3}=0,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the first coefficient is nonzero, so the set is linearly dependent. In general, any set that contains a zero-vector is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n3{t}^{2}-t=0\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot t+3\\cdot {t}^{2}+0\\cdot {t}^{3}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the set is not linearly independent, it can't form a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360515 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124592 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2588e089-4786-5346-b42d-65c2740ae2ab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Sets of Vectors in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17155733-9ce3-5dd6-84a2-3799b6de919b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452131} {:answer/id #uuid "dfcbd7ad-62b9-5a5a-ae56-b789911230aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfcbd7ad-62b9-5a5a-ae56-b789911230aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452132} :answer-field/id #uuid "98805a85-3b6d-5ca6-ada0-5674aa14b825" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452913} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "032cab00-e88f-578f-82a6-78ad15f292ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452133} {:answer/id #uuid "bfaea224-86ea-5be7-81b2-96ffa8441385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfaea224-86ea-5be7-81b2-96ffa8441385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452134} :answer-field/id #uuid "64571fa1-9211-5a32-a07a-f6d759efd7bb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452914} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4a0b18d-16c0-524b-b6eb-f80d6f5f2adf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452135} {:answer/id #uuid "b48aff0a-c3a2-5b11-883a-17cbbaa86041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b48aff0a-c3a2-5b11-883a-17cbbaa86041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452136} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcb4e9fc-eea8-5d96-91cc-58151af98234" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b873442b-9d2d-5d41-a7b6-d67882fe4b7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94848" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{3}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ over $R$ with degrees at most $3.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\{1,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{3}[t]$\n\n- **II.** ${t}^{3}-3t+8$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{1,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$\n\n- **III.** $\\{1,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}_{3}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the equation \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot 1+{x}_{2}\\cdot t+{x}_{3}\\cdot {t}^{2}+{x}_{4}\\cdot {t}^{3}=0,\n$$\n\n \nis true if and only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0.$ So, the set is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n{t}^{3}-3t+8=8\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot t+0\\cdot {t}^{2}+1\\cdot {t}^{3}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the set is linearly independent and for any polynomial in ${R}_{3}[t],$ we get \n\n$$\na{t}^{3}+b{t}^{2}+ct+d=d\\cdot 1+c\\cdot t+b\\cdot {t}^{2}+a\\cdot {t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360516 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124592 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2588e089-4786-5346-b42d-65c2740ae2ab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Sets of Vectors in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1429c0a-89af-5805-8580-b73e7cd5d01a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452137} {:answer/id #uuid "624e0c32-5d2c-56d6-81a3-b8d4282b2eb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1429c0a-89af-5805-8580-b73e7cd5d01a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452137} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e7b7fcb-d746-5098-8534-b43bcfff8673" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452916} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e3f86b7-428b-5f3c-96de-c85c2894488b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452139} {:answer/id #uuid "52cc4177-3ee9-5140-bd61-3db7f9ff2e16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52cc4177-3ee9-5140-bd61-3db7f9ff2e16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452140} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9c6abba-e799-5070-8c49-022c9a387a3f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452917} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6e785fe-8b18-56e6-9291-7b0b3e83aeef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452141} {:answer/id #uuid "b145c6d5-7d89-5fe4-b6c1-fa9b85036ee7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6e785fe-8b18-56e6-9291-7b0b3e83aeef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452141} :answer-field/id #uuid "4105ae7e-75bf-54ba-80a7-8977f2a90571" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bf9e33e0-00b4-5d7d-a1a7-55573563c2a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-94850" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{3}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ over $R$ with degrees at most $3.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\{0,{t}^{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{3}[t]$\n\n- **II.** $-{t}^{3}$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{0,{t}^{3}\\}$\n\n- **III.** $\\{0,{t}^{3}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}_{3}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot {t}^{3}=0,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the first coefficient is nonzero, so the set is linearly dependent. In general, any set that contains a zero-vector is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n-{t}^{3}=0\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot {t}^{3}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the set is not linearly independent, it can't form a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360519 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124489 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "073042ee-d96d-5872-9681-ddcea43a2d37" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Sets of Vectors in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c0f5ce7-fdc1-5450-becc-3455d6e589d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452143} {:answer/id #uuid "9eaa2dd6-e820-58e5-8ff1-8304461c433e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9eaa2dd6-e820-58e5-8ff1-8304461c433e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452144} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9afc791-a8b1-53ee-ad26-58720715d425" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452919} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0fa1020-fa7b-566a-9214-2bd81560930f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452145} {:answer/id #uuid "b0aa9cd6-3ac4-5030-bdf4-5675f4a824c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0aa9cd6-3ac4-5030-bdf4-5675f4a824c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452146} :answer-field/id #uuid "71c4e941-084c-5fca-9534-f53207480cf7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452920} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ec842c7-f3d8-5abd-9a36-6e857fae461a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452147} {:answer/id #uuid "33859395-8ac6-5662-ade7-d42fc98ae264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ec842c7-f3d8-5abd-9a36-6e857fae461a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452147} :answer-field/id #uuid "df7c3d55-f90b-5b9f-a9ed-d059376c3d11" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0064f075-2267-5e41-8556-443f519b3150" :question/math-academy-id "q-94859" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]}$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- **II.** $[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ can be expressed as a linear combination of ${[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]}$\n- **III.** ${[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis true if and only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ So, the set is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]=2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+0\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ can't be written as a linear combination of \n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nsince all these linear combinations result in matrices with the entry ${a}_{12}=0:$\n\n$$\na\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+b\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2b\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}]}
